C03: the near-miss application question names the installed candidates and never echoes the misspelt name (APPS1499)

APPS1497 measured that «Abre stea,» and «Sí, abre Ste.» asked «¿Querés que abra Steam?», but «abres team» (Microsoft Teams and Steam) and both «Steel» literals failed: the validator demanded each full catalog name and the model echoed «Steel» instead of writing Steam, so the App recovered with generic questions. The clarifier's situation now lists the installed candidates exactly and forbids repeating the person's misspelt name (with a spelled-out example in the corrected retry), and the validator accepts a distinctive token of a name («Teams» for «Microsoft Teams»), ignoring vendor words.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


